One module whose two packages carry references a configured root or a pattern
can name: two functions, a type with a member of each kind, a blank declaration
that borrows the package's reference, and a nested package.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/patterns

go 1.27.1
-- catalog.go --
package patterns

// Alpha is named by an exact configured root.
func Alpha() string { return "alpha" }

// Beta is named by no configured root.
func Beta() string { return "beta" }

// Box carries one field and one method.
type Box struct {
	Lid int
}

// Open reports the lid.
func (b Box) Open() int { return b.Lid }

var _ = Beta()
-- inner/inner.go --
package inner

// Gamma sits one path element below the module root.
func Gamma() string { return "gamma" }
